  "script": "Google now pings shoppers the second your product is back in stock. But it only knows what your data tells it. 3 checks so that alert actually fires. First, compare your warehouse count to your store count today. Warehouse says 40, store says 0? Google says sold out, and the alert never goes out. Second, check how often your stock syncs. Once a night is too slow in peak. Aim for every hour. Third, make your price and shipping time match everywhere. 16 in 100 shoppers now start in ChatGPT, and assistants read your data, not your homepage. Keeping that in sync is what we build at Content Systems.ai. Want us to check yours? Free quote, link in bio.",
